  "status_text": "Could two machines agree on every short word and give different answers on a long one? Each reads letters from the same finite alphabet and stores six numbers over the same field, with linear updates and a linear readout. Agreement on every word of at most eleven letters guarantees agreement forever. If the reachable states span each memory and every nonzero state can affect a future output, exactly one linear change of coordinates matches their starts, updates and outputs. Lean checked both known results (L-lib-545, L-lib-550).",
